{"format":1,"seq":290,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Though the user asked to make a release, the documented process has the maintainer review before publishing, so I should leave this as a draft and flag it for review rather than publishing it outright.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I merged #83 and released v2.5.2. The GitHub Release is still a draft for you to review and publish ([Releases](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/releases)), as `CONTRIBUTING.md` asks.\n\n- **#83:** squash-merged as `ccc0452`. Before merging, I updated its description: the job summary no longer shows the thread commands in any mode.\n- **#84 (`chore: release 2.5.2`):** sets the version to 2.5.2. CI passed and I squash-merged it as `753f110`.\n- **Tag:** I pushed the annotated tag `v2.5.2` on `753f110`. `release.yml` succeeded: it created the draft release and moved `v2` to `753f110`, so `cv/pi-action@v2` now points to 2.5.2.\n\nThe release covers #81, #82 and #83, which were all `feat:` changes, but I kept it a patch release as you asked. The notes in #84:\n- **Added:** tools of pi-durable extensions can set how the workflow log shows their calls (`present`).\n- **Changed:**\n  - pit calls show their label in the log; this needs pit 0.36.5 or later.\n  - Each comment now ends with a collapsed section with the commands that read its thread, and the job summary no longer shows them."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":535,"cacheRead":39074,"cacheWrite":531,"totalTokens":40142,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":109},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1794636900481,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_w4upt3owku4n76z6u27elwkgf4pdqdwh7o5fatv7cpndnxopyd6q","rawStopReason":"end_turn","durationMs":11413,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.a